# The hint writer stops (session ended, compositor restarted without its
# script, a desktop without one) and leaves an empty snapshot: hints are off.
# By default the policy runs with hints only, so it stopped altogether, and
# what it had moved out stayed in sysmem for as long as the process lived,
# drawing over PCIe. Wanted: it comes back as room allows (the policy
# without hints: an active process as soon as it fits), nothing more goes out.
cap 6000
set auto 2
set compact 0
proc 1614 kwin_wayland old
proc 2837 chrome old
proc 2210 ghostty old
act 1614 0 4
alloc 1614 250 n=5 fixed
alloc 2837 1200
alloc 2210 300
hint 1614 v
hint 2837 h
hint 2210 f
act 2837 60 0
act 2210 0 10
at 5
mark the terminal grows: hidden Chrome makes room
alloc 2210 3800 n=8
at 10
expect sys 2837 > 0

mark the terminal frees its memory, the writer stops
free 2210 3800
set hints 0
act 2837 0 10                # Chrome is used again (no window state known)
at 20
expect sys 2837 == 0
expect evicts 2210 == 0
